## p1-px1 | Phys 1 exam practice: kinematics and forces | physics | 1 | phys1 | p1-nl
quiz 2 | A car accelerates from rest at 3 m/s² for 4 s. Final speed?
* 12 m/s
o 7 m/s
o 24 m/s
o 0.75 m/s
= v = u + at = 0 + 12.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Same car: distance covered in those 4 s?
* 24 m
o 12 m
o 48 m
o 6 m
= s = ½at² = ½ × 3 × 16.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A ball is thrown up at 20 m/s (g = 10). Maximum height?
* 20 m
o 40 m
o 10 m
o 2 m
= v² = u² − 2gh: h = 400/20.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A 10 kg box on a 30° frictionless slope. Acceleration down the slope? (g = 10)
* 5 m/s²
o 10 m/s²
o 8.7 m/s²
o 0 m/s²
= a = g sin 30°.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Kinetic friction μ = 0.2 on a 5 kg block sliding on a level floor. Friction force? (g = 10)
* 10 N
o 1 N
o 50 N
o 25 N
= F = μmg = 0.2 × 50.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | A 1,200 kg car rounds a 40 m radius bend at 10 m/s. Required centripetal force?
* 3,000 N
o 300 N
o 30,000 N
o 1,200 N
= mv²/r = 1200 × 100/40.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A projectile is launched horizontally at 15 m/s from a 20 m cliff (g = 10). How far out does it land?
* 30 m
o 15 m
o 20 m
o 45 m
= Fall time √(2 × 20/10) = 2 s. Horizontal: 15 × 2.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Weight of a 70 kg astronaut on the Moon (g = 1.6 m/s²)?
* 112 N
o 70 N
o 700 N
o 11 N
= W = mg. Mass stays 70 kg everywhere.
> Energy and momentum practice next

## p1-px2 | Phys 1 exam practice: energy, momentum, rotation | physics | 1 | phys1 | p1-mom
quiz 3 | A 2 kg trolley at 3 m/s. Kinetic energy?
* 9 J
o 6 J
o 18 J
o 3 J
= ½mv² = ½ × 2 × 9.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A 60 kg climber gains 500 m of height. Gain in potential energy? (g = 10)
* 300 kJ
o 30 kJ
o 3 MJ
o 3 kJ
= mgh = 60 × 10 × 500 = 300,000 J.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A 5 kg gun fires a 0.01 kg bullet at 500 m/s. Recoil speed?
* 1 m/s
o 5 m/s
o 0.1 m/s
o 100 m/s
= Momentum: 0.01 × 500 = 5 × v.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | A 0.15 kg ball hits a wall at 20 m/s and rebounds at 20 m/s. Impulse magnitude?
* 6 N s
o 3 N s
o 0
o 1.5 N s
= Δp = 0.15 × (20 − (−20)).
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A motor lifts 100 kg by 10 m in 20 s. Power output? (g = 10)
* 500 W
o 1,000 W
o 5,000 W
o 50 W
= mgh/t = 10,000/20.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | A disc (I = ½MR²) of mass 2 kg, radius 0.5 m spins at 10 rad/s. Rotational KE?
* 12.5 J
o 25 J
o 5 J
o 50 J
= I = 0.25 kg m². KE = ½Iω² = ½ × 0.25 × 100.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | A spring (k = 400 N/m) with a 1 kg mass. Period of oscillation?
* π/10 s ≈ 0.31 s
o 20 s
o 2π s
o 0.05 s
= T = 2π√(m/k) = 2π/20.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Orbital speed of a satellite in low Earth orbit (r ≈ 6,700 km, g there ≈ 8.9 m/s²)?
* About 7.7 km/s
o About 11 km/s
o About 3 km/s
o About 30 km/s
= v = √(g r) = √(8.9 × 6.7 × 10⁶) ≈ 7.7 km/s.
> E&M practice next

## p2-px1 | Phys 2 exam practice | physics | 1 | phys2 | p2-dc
quiz 3 | Force between charges of 2 μC and 3 μC, 0.3 m apart? (k = 9 × 10⁹)
* 0.6 N
o 6 N
o 0.06 N
o 60 N
= F = 9 × 10⁹ × 6 × 10⁻¹²/0.09 = 0.6 N.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A 3 μF capacitor at 100 V. Charge stored?
* 300 μC
o 30 μC
o 3 mC
o 0.03 μC
= Q = CV.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Energy stored in that capacitor?
* 15 mJ
o 30 mJ
o 150 mJ
o 1.5 mJ
= ½CV² = ½ × 3 × 10⁻⁶ × 10⁴ = 0.015 J.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A 2 kW kettle runs on 230 V. Current drawn?
* About 8.7 A
o About 0.12 A
o About 460 A
o About 2 A
= I = P/V = 2000/230.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Resistance of that kettle's element?
* About 26 Ω
o About 0.04 Ω
o About 460 Ω
o About 2.6 Ω
= R = V²/P = 52,900/2000.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Field 5 cm from a long wire carrying 10 A? (μ₀ = 4π × 10⁻⁷)
* 40 μT
o 4 μT
o 400 μT
o 0.4 μT
= B = μ₀I/(2πr) = 2 × 10⁻⁷ × 10/0.05.
= Comparable to Earth's field (about 50 μT).
> Next problem

quiz 4 | A proton moves at 10⁶ m/s perpendicular to a 0.1 T field. Radius of its circle? (m = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg)
* About 10 cm
o About 1 mm
o About 1 m
o About 10 m
= r = mv/(qB) = (1.67 × 10⁻²¹)/(1.6 × 10⁻²⁰) ≈ 0.10 m.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A 500-turn coil of area 0.01 m² in a field that drops from 0.2 T to 0 in 0.05 s. Average EMF?
* 20 V
o 2 V
o 0.2 V
o 200 V
= ε = NAΔB/Δt = 500 × 0.01 × 0.2/0.05.
> Phys 3 practice next

## p3-px1 | Phys 3 exam practice | physics | 2 | phys3 | p3-oldq
quiz 3 | Energy of a photon with wavelength 600 nm? (hc ≈ 1240 eV·nm)
* About 2.1 eV
o About 0.5 eV
o About 21 eV
o About 600 eV
= E = hc/λ = 1240/600.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Hydrogen electron drops from n = 2 to n = 1. Photon energy?
* 10.2 eV
o 13.6 eV
o 3.4 eV
o 6.8 eV
= 13.6(1 − 1/4).
= That's the ultraviolet Lyman-alpha line, 122 nm.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A muon's lifetime at rest is 2.2 μs. At γ = 10, how long does it last in the lab frame?
* 22 μs
o 0.22 μs
o 2.2 μs
o 220 μs
= Time dilation: γτ.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | A half-life of 6 hours. Fraction left after 1 day?
* 1/16
o 1/4
o 1/24
o 1/8
= 24/6 = 4 half-lives: (1/2)⁴.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Rest energy of an electron?
* 511 keV
o 938 MeV
o 13.6 eV
o 1 MeV
= mc² for the electron. 938 MeV is the proton's.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | de Broglie wavelength of an electron accelerated through 100 V? (h/√(2me·V) ≈ 1.23 nm/√V)
* About 0.12 nm
o About 1.2 nm
o About 12 nm
o About 0.012 nm
= 1.23/√100 = 0.123 nm: similar to atomic spacings, so electrons diffract off crystals.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | A Carnot fridge between −3°C and 27°C. Maximum coefficient of performance?
* 9
o 10
o 0.9
o 1.1
= COP = T_c/(T_h − T_c) = 270/30.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Particle in a box: ground state 0.5 eV. Energy of the photon emitted in the 2 → 1 transition?
* 1.5 eV
o 0.5 eV
o 2 eV
o 1 eV
= E₂ = 4 × 0.5 = 2 eV. Difference 1.5 eV.
> All physics practice sets done
